The cargo [package] name and version in Cargo.toml determine the built binary's filename and --version output, while packages/cli/package.json's bin and optionalDependencies plus the postinstall installer's hardcoded binary names and platform-package lookups must mirror them; scripts/sync-versions.sh is the authority that fans the package.json version out to Cargo.toml, the npm platform packages, and Cargo.lock, so a manual version or name edit on one side alone ships a mismatched release.
